From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:33:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the video call media path against live WhatsApp clients

Changes made while bringing up 1:1 video calls between a webOS device
and the official Android client:

- answer relaylatency probes for calls we place, not only for calls we
  receive; the event fires in both directions
- reply to a peer's request to turn video on with an explicit upgrade
  accept, otherwise the official client times the request out
- send an ICE Binding Request carrying the relay token before DTLS, and
  close the relay channel as soon as the call context ends instead of
  leaking its socket and keep-alive
- use one RTCP CNAME for audio and video, send SR+SDES as soon as the
  relay allocation succeeds, and keep sending PLI at the peer's video
  SSRC until (and briefly after) its first frame
- RTP, H.264 packetisation, STUN and signalling adjustments to match
  captures of the official client
- the signalling and relay paths log the raw stanzas and relay details
  used to diagnose the above
- whatsmeow is required at v0.0.0-20260716095330-85d99080dee8 for
  binary.Node.String()

The tests TestVideoHeaderMatchesAndroidCapture, TestOfferAdvertisesVideo
and engine_media_test.go (newMediaSrtcpSender's new argument) still
expect the old values and are not updated here.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
